SRCK_R_20 {
    @ Designers should refer to the seal ring layout (Fig. 1), which should include AA, CT, Mn(n=1~8), TM1, TM2, TKM, Vn(n=1~7), TV1, TV2 to provide a low resistance path to ground for surge currents
    X = NET AREA RATIO MARKS AAS CTS M1S_RING V1S M2S_RING V2S M3S_RING V3S M4S_RING V4S M5S_RING V5S M6S_RING TV2S TKMS_RING > 0 [!!(AREA(AAS))*!!(AREA(CTS))*!!(AREA(M1S_RING))*!!(AREA(V1S))*!!(AREA(M2S_RING))*!!(AREA(V2S))*!!(AREA(M3S_RING))*!!(AREA(V3S))*!!(AREA(M4S_RING))*!!(AREA(V4S))*!!(AREA(M5S_RING))*!!(AREA(V5S))*!!(AREA(M6S_RING))*!!(AREA(TV2S))*!!(AREA(TKMS_RING))]
    (MARKS NOT X) NOT INSIDE EXCLUi
    Y = NET AREA RATIO RDLS_RING BCB1S TKMS_RING > 0 [!!(AREA(TKMS_RING))*!!(AREA(BCB1S))*!!(AREA(RDLS_RING))]
    ((MARKS ENCLOSE RDL) NOT ENCLOSE Y) NOT INSIDE EXCLUi
    Z = NET AREA RATIO BCB1S RDLS_RING TKMS_RING > 0 [!!(AREA(TKMS_RING))*!!(AREA(BCB1S))*!!(AREA(RDLS_RING))]
    ((MARKS ENCLOSE BCB1) NOT ENCLOSE Z) NOT INSIDE EXCLUi
}
